{{Quote|Seems to me that the weakness in the Empire is in men like you, Moff Pandion. Paltry, ineffectual idiots. Men who want to be leaders more than they want to actually lead. And besides, what is a moff anyway? A meager sector head. Even the name sounds weak. Moff. Moff. It's the sound a dog makes as it regurgitates its dinner&mdash;|[[Sinjir Rath Velus]], to Moff [[Valco Pandion]]|<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref>}}
'''Moff''' was the [[Politics|political]] rank held by the [[governor]]s of each [[sector]] in the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="Tarkin" /> A collective body called the [[Council of Moffs]] was created by [[Galactic Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]].<ref name="Palpatine" /> Moffs also acted as [[Imperial officer|military officers]]. As such, as the power of the [[Imperial Senate]] deteriorated and that authority was instead invested within Moffs,<ref name="RiseFall">''[[Star Wars: The Rise and Fall of the Galactic Empire]]''</ref> the Empire transformed into a [[stratocracy]].<ref name="Rogue One Visual Guide">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: The Ultimate Visual Guide]]''</ref>

==History==
{{Quote|Meet Moff Tarkin, crime lord. Sector governor of Greater Seswenna and more.|[[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] introduces Moff Tarkin to [[Faazah]]|<ref name="Tarkin" />}}
[[File:Tarkin-Vader.jpg|thumb|left|200px|More powerful than a regular Moff due to his favor with Emperor Sheev Palpatine, Moff Wilhuff Tarkin held great influence in the Empire.]]
Following the [[Proclamation of the New Order|creation]] of the [[Galactic Empire]], [[Galactic Emperor|Emperor]] [[Darth Sidious|Palpatine]] conferred the new order of [[military rank|rank]], the moff, to around a dozen of the Empire's most valued [[Imperial officer|officers]] and regional [[commander]]s. [[Wilhuff Tarkin]] was one such individual, despite already having been promoted to the rank of [[admiral]] at the end of the [[Clone War]]s and serving as [[governor]], the latter of which remained his Despite his preferred title. Following his promotion, Tarkin advocated that moffs entrusted with sector control,<ref name="Catalyst">''[[Catalyst: A Rogue One Novel]]''</ref> which eventually became a reality by [[14 BBY]].<ref name="Tarkin" />

Also by the fifteenth [[Standard year|year]] of the [[Imperial Era|Empire's reign]], the amount of moffs had grown to a fixed number of twenty, all of whom answered to the [[Imperial Ruling Council]]. That same year, the senior rank of [[Grand Moff]] was created and awarded to Wilhuff Tarkin.<ref name="Tarkin" /> Palpatine also established the [[Council of Moffs]] around that [[time]].<ref name="Palpatine" /> As a symbol of their charge, Moffs wore a [[rank insignia plaque]] bearing ten [[color]]ed squares: five blue over three red and two gold<ref name="SWI 153">{{InsiderCite|153|Tarkin Revealed}}</ref> or twelve squares: six blue over three red and three gold.<ref name="Thrawn 3">[[Thrawn 3|''Thrawn'' 3]]</ref> Moffs could use four [[code cylinder]]s, with two on each pocket.<ref name="Tarkin" />

In the aftermath of the [[Battle of Endor]], Moff [[Valco Pandion]] proclaimed himself a Grand Moff<ref name="Aftermath" /> and tried to assemble his [[Valco Pandion's fleet|own fleet]].<ref name="Alphabet Squadron" /> Further into the [[New Republic Era]],<ref name="Chapter 8" /> [[Gideon]] led a sizeable [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]]<ref name="GideonTopps">{{Topps|set=2022 Topps Finest Star Wars|cardname=Moff Gideon}}</ref> under his title of moff.<ref name="Chapter 8" />

==Role, duties, and powers==
{{Quote|&hellip;I also know who they ''say'' you are. The Fiend of Castell. The Burning Moff. The Imperial Governor of this sector, ''brutal'' in your response to even the slightest challenge to the Empire's authority.''"<br />"''I am an extension of the Emperor's will. My actions here simply execute his directives. The Emperor is the mind. I am his tool. Is a ''tool'' responsible if it is used to kill someone?|Lando Calrissian and Moff Ssaria|<ref name="Lando 1">[[Lando 1|''Lando'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:Uprising-Loading-Screen-Empire.png|thumb|right|300px|As the governors of an Imperial sector, moffs held command over Sector Groups, a formation of Imperial military and intelligence assets to ensure order in their territory]]
Originally created as a rank in the [[Galactic Empire]] for [[Darth Sidious|the]] [[Emperor]] to give to his most valued [[officers]] and regional [[commanders]],<ref name="Catalyst" /> the moffs were eventually entrusted with the role of [[governor|governing]] [[Sector|star sectors]]<ref name="Tarkin">[[Tarkin (novel)|''Tarkin'']]</ref> following the advocacy of Moff [[Wilhuff Tarkin|Tarkin]].<ref name="Catalyst" /> In this arrangement, Imperial leadership in a given sector resided in the sector's moff, who was primarily responsible for the security of the sector. To achieve this, moffs held command over [[Sector Group]]s, a formation made up of military and intelligence assets for a given sector.<ref name="Dawn">''[[Dawn of Rebellion]]''</ref> Included in these sector groups were Twenty-four [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|''Imperial''-class Star Destroyers]] that made up the [[Sector fleet]] such as the [[Lothal sector fleet]] and the [[Adelhard's fleet|Anoat sector fleet]], which moffs also held authority over.<ref name="BMF 20">{{BuildFalconCite|20|Starship Fact File}}</ref> While most [[planetary Governor|planetary governors]] fell under the command of sector moffs, on occasion, planetary governors held the rank of moff themself.<ref name="Dawn" />

[[Star system]]s and sectors that showed signs of unrest or insurgent activity were grouped together into [[oversector]]s, the authority of which fell under the command of a [[Grand Moff]]. Those who held the senior rank of Grand Moff had a great deal of freedom to suppress troublesome areas in their oversector, including the ability of overrule any moff or planetary governor under the command. Moffs were appointed by either the [[Galactic Emperor]] himself or by one of his [[Emperor's adviser|advisors]],<ref name="Dawn" /> including the [[supreme commander of the Imperial fleet]] [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]],<ref name="IR1 rising">{{StoryCite|story=The Rising|book=Battle of Jakku &mdash; Insurgency Rising 1}}</ref> though moffs ultimately answered to both.<ref name="Dawn" />

==Uniform and Equipment==
[[File:Gideon-AG-Crop-Clean.png|thumb|left|150px|The battle armor worn by Moff Gideon during the New Republic Era]]
Moffs of the [[Galactic Empire]] wore green-grey [[Imperial officer's uniform]]s with<ref name="TPOA">{{TOTE|The Path of Anger}}</ref><ref name="naboocharacters">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Heroes of Naboo and Other Characters of the Galaxy}}</ref> two<ref name="TPOA" /> or four [[code cylinder]]s,<ref name="naboocharacters" /> a black belt, and black boots. While some moffs did not wear an [[Imperial kepi]],<ref name="Age of Rebellion">[[Age of Rebellion - Darth Vader 1|''Age of Rebellion - Darth Vader'' 1]]</ref><ref name="TPOA" /> Moff [[Derrek Raythe]] wore a kepi with an [[officer's disk]],<ref name="Battlefront II">''[[Star Wars Battlefront II]]''</ref> as did Moff [[Tiaan Jerjerrod]].<ref name="RotJ">{{Film|VI}}</ref> Over their left [[breast]], Moffs wore a [[Rank insignia plaque]] with six blue tiles on the top row and three red tiles followed by three yellow tiles on the bottom row.<ref name="Allies and Adversaries">''[[Allies and Adversaries]]''</ref> Early in the Empire's reign, Moffs could also use plaques with five blue tiles that sat above three red tiles followed by two yellow tiles to signify their rank and title.<ref name="Tarkin Revealed">{{InsiderCite|153|Tarkin Revealed}}</ref>

While serving as a moff of the [[Anoat sector]], [[Ubrik Adelhard]] wore a unique Imperial officer's uniform that was black from the neck down to the chest, and white below the chest. Additionally, Adelhard wore a grey epaulette on each shoulder, a pair of black gloves, a black and dark grey belt, and a pair of black boots.<ref name="Ewoks1" /> While in private with [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]], Moff [[Ssaria]] did not wear an Imperial officer's uniform, instead opting to wear casual clothes.<ref name="Lando 1" /> After the [[Battle of Jakku]] fall of the Galactic Empire, Moff [[Gideon]] of the [[neo-Imperial forces|Imperial Remnant]] wore an [[Clothing|outfit]] similar to an [[Imperial military uniforms|Imperial uniform]] with dark-[[color]]ed reflective [[Imperial officer battle armor|battle armor]] and a black [[cape]].<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> Gideon later wore a full [[Dark Trooper phase 4|full suit of armor]] made in a similar style as [[Mandalorian armor]] and was based on his third-generation Dark Troopers that was made of [[beskar]] during the [[Liberation of Mandalore|Last Battle for Mandalore]]. The armor's left vambrace was equipped with a [[Wrist rocket|rocket launcher]] and a [[whipcord launcher]] while the right vambrace was equipped with a [[Wrist blaster|blaster]] and a [[flamethrower]]. The suit's helmet crowned Mandalorian-style helmet as well as a [[jetpack]].<ref name="Chapter 24">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
In [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi|''Star Wars'': Episode VI ''Return of the Jedi'']], Moff [[Tiaan Jerjerrod|Jerjerrod]] wore the rank plaque of a [[commander]]<ref name="Hidalgo Tweet Rank plaques">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/722602214594752513|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|quote=@StompinSteveB No, everyone's is wrong in ROTJ. It was EVERYONE IS A COMMANDER DAY at Endor.|nobackup=1}}</ref> due to a costuming error.<ref name="25 years">{{InsiderCite|105|25 Years of Return of the Jedi!|25 Years of ''Return of the Jedi''!}}</ref> The rank badge specific to Moffs was first depicted in an illustration by [[Joe Corroney]] for ''[[Tarkin Revealed]]'', an article by [[Michael Kogge]] that was published in [[Star Wars Insider 153|''Star Wars Insider'' 153]].<ref name="SWI 153" />

